Has the original rename-from-just-to-single been applied? No.  
Here’s what still needs to change in Registry.java:

1. Rename the two `just` methods to `single`:  
   - Lines 344–346:  
     ```java
     // before
     static Registry just(Object object) {
       return registry().add(object).build();
     }
     // after
     static Registry single(Object object) {
       return registry().add(object).build();
     }
     ```
   - Lines 357–359:  
     ```java
     // before
     static <T> Registry just(Class<? super T> publicType, T implementation) {
       return registry().add(publicType, implementation).build();
     }
     // after
     static <T> Registry single(Class<? super T> publicType, T implementation) {
       return registry().add(publicType, implementation).build();
     }
     ```

2. Update the JavaDoc examples that refer to `just` (around lines 39 and 51):  
   - Change  
     `import static ratpack.registry.Registry.just;`  
     to  
     `import static ratpack.registry.Registry.single;`  
   - Change  
     `context.next(just(new Thing("foo")));`  
     to  
     `context.next(single(new Thing("foo")));`

After making those changes, the API will expose only `single(...)` for single‐entry registries.  
