46:  * These supporting objects can be managed by Guice and made available to handlers (either by dependency injection or registry lookup)
47:  * for increased reusability, modularity and testability.
48:  * <p>
49:  * The Guice integration is not part of the Ratpack core library, but is available as a separate add on.
50:  * That said, Ratpack is designed to support something like Guice as an integral piece via it's {@link Registry} abstraction.
51:  * Guice is the “official” solution.
52:  * </p>
53:  * <h3>Starting a Guice Ratpack app</h3>
54:  * <p>
55:  * The user entry point for Ratpack applications is the {@link ratpack.launch.HandlerFactory} implementation
56:  * that is given to the {@link ratpack.launch.LaunchConfigBuilder#build(ratpack.launch.HandlerFactory)} method.
57:  * This implementation can use one of the {@code handler(...) } static methods.
58:  * <p>
59:  * Below is a complete example for bootstrapping a Guice based Ratpack application.
60:  * </p>
